Another way to think about probability is to imagine a game of chance, like rolling a die. If the die has six sides, each with a different number on it, then there are six possible outcomes. The probability of getting a particular outcome, such as rolling a 5, is 1/6. This is because there is one favorable outcome out of the six possible numbers on the die.

Probability can also be expressed as a percentage. For example, if the probability of getting heads when flipping a coin is 50%, then the probability expressed as a percentage is 50%. This is another way to represent the same information, just in a different format using percentages instead of fractions.

