```

The idea is to divide the problem into two subproblems: finding the number of full binary trees with n-1 vertices and the number of full binary trees with n-2 vertices. This approach involves breaking down the main problem into smaller, more manageable parts. We then combine the solutions of these subproblems using the formula (a + b) // 2, which gives the number of full binary trees with n vertices. Essentially, this formula helps in determining the number of full binary trees by calculating the average of the solutions to the subproblems. The recursive nature of the solution is key to its implementation.

